{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"Updated the compatibility boundary in [adapter.py](/workspace/in/shopmono/packages/orders/orders/adapter.py) so `orders` now accepts both the new `catalog` price model and legacy product dictionaries. It reads `Product.price.amount_cents` and `Product.price.currency` for current objects, still supports legacy `price_cents`, and also handles dictionary inputs carrying the new nested `price` shape. Mixed-currency validation remains in [service.py](/workspace/in/shopmono/packages/orders/orders/service.py) and still raises a clear `ValueError`.\n\nI also wrote the required report to [interface_fix_report.md](/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md).\n\nVerification: the exact requested command could not run in this container because `python` is not installed, and `python3 -m pytest tests` failed because `pytest` is unavailable here. I did run an equivalent manual verification with `python3` and the repo `PYTHONPATH`, covering new `Money` products, legacy dicts, report aggregation, and mixed-currency rejection."}}
